WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.700
Lock out, and tag out. Six steps, every
time, before you service a machine.

00:00:07.541 --> 00:00:13.181
Step one. Prepare. Know every energy
source on this machine: electrical,

00:00:13.181 --> 00:00:18.601
hydraulic, air, and anything stored in
springs or raised parts. Tell everyone

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:20.801
nearby that it is going down.

00:00:22.373 --> 00:00:25.653
Step two. Shut it down with the normal
stop control.

00:00:27.452 --> 00:00:32.892
Step three. Isolate it. Open the main
disconnect, and close the supply valves.

00:00:34.761 --> 00:00:37.481
Step four. Lock and tag every isolation

00:00:37.481 --> 00:00:41.401
point. Your lock, your tag, your key.
Nobody else's.

00:00:43.592 --> 00:00:49.432
Step five. Release stored energy. Bleed
off pressure in the lines, block or lower

00:00:49.432 --> 00:00:52.172
raised parts, and let capacitors
discharge.

00:00:54.174 --> 00:00:57.934
Step six. Verify. Press start. Nothing

00:00:57.934 --> 00:01:00.514
should move. Then return the control to
off.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:06.200
If anything moves, stop. Step away, and
report it.
